index c4b4ea9..9cc5e8e 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,12 +2,12 @@
 
 Trusted host plugin for the OR3 workflow editor and chat execution. It keeps the existing `workflow-entry` post type, `workflow-execution` message discriminator, and `or3-workflow-saved`/`or3-workflow-autosave` local-storage keys. No data migration is intended.
 
-The package owns its pane, sidebar, message renderer, editor extensions, send controller, activity source, model sync, image caption decisions, generated-image routing, background execution engine, workflow catalog, run journal, and HITL coordination. The host supplies guarded ports for storage, model and tool access, authentication, sync, background jobs, and notifications. Installed Workflows UI and server routes are served from this package; disabling it removes its UI contributions.
+The package owns its pane, sidebar, message renderer, editor extensions, send controller, activity source, model sync, image caption decisions, generated-image routing, background execution engine, workflow catalog, run journal, and HITL coordination. The public SDK supplies scoped posts and messages, AI provider/model access, enabled tools, background jobs and lifecycle hooks. Installed Workflows UI and server routes are served from this package; disabling it removes its UI contributions.
 
 The host's workflow settings govern package activation, slash commands, and execution. Stop cancels the selected active run. When activated after a reload, the package marks unfinished foreground runs as interrupted so their cards can resume from a checkpoint. Message persistence stays bound to the workspace that activated the plugin.
 
-The package interprets raw, type-scoped host records in `src/core/workflowLoad.ts`: metadata validation, lookup/search, interrupted-run decisions, Activity records, and conversation-history projection. Startup reconciliation uses conditional message clocks so it cannot overwrite a concurrently updated run. Message renderers and editor extensions register through the SDK contribution mechanism. The host retains the older private callbacks for already-installed artifacts; the new client uses `records` instead. Model/tool execution, background jobs, generated-image persistence, and shell UI still use the temporary host bridge.
+The package interprets raw, type-scoped host records in `src/core/workflowLoad.ts`: metadata validation, lookup/search, interrupted-run decisions, Activity records, and conversation-history projection. Startup reconciliation uses conditional message clocks so it cannot overwrite a concurrently updated run. Message renderers and editor extensions register through the SDK contribution mechanism. The SDK adapter supplies raw records; interpretation remains in the package. The pane and renderer register before interrupted-run reconciliation. Shell UI comes from `ui.kit`; generated images use `files.write` and `chat.messages.attachFile`. Version 0.2.0 requires SDK 2.1 and `or3-trusted-ui-kit-v1`, `or3-trusted-host-v2`, and `or3-trusted-chat-records-v1`. The `ai.provider` grant exposes the configured raw API key and must be reviewed accordingly. Server handlers retrieve dispatcher-authorized services through `getPluginServerContext`.
 
-Run `bun run validate`, `bun run typecheck`, `bun run build`, `bun run test:routes`, `bun run test:continuity`, and `bun run pack` from this directory before installing a package artifact. The route test executes the built background and HITL handlers with local host ports and no model request. The continuity fixture loads existing workflow and execution rows to verify stop and retry. To create an installable ZIP, run `bun node_modules/@or3/plugin-sdk/bin/or3-plugin.mjs pack . --archive /absolute/path/workflows.zip` after building. The `.or3-sdk` directory is the pinned source dependency used for clean builds; the plugin archive excludes it.
+Run `bun run validate`, `bun run typecheck`, `bun run build`, `bun run test:routes`, `bun run test:continuity`, and `bun run pack` from this directory before installing a package artifact. The route test executes the built background and HITL handlers with local host ports and no model request. The continuity fixture loads existing workflow and execution rows to verify stop and retry. To create an installable ZIP, run `bun node_modules/@or3/plugin-sdk/bin/or3-plugin.mjs pack . --archive /absolute/path/workflows.zip` after building. Development uses the sibling SDK package; runtime archives use the host SDK external and exclude development dependencies.
 
-This checkout is pinned at package version `0.1.1`. Use `bun install --frozen-lockfile` before qualification. Keep `package.json` and `or3.manifest.json` on the same fresh version for each new artifact; a different archive with changed bytes needs a new version before release. This package is private and is installed through OR3's reviewed package flow, not the creator's build-time provider version map.
+This checkout is pinned at package version `0.2.0`. Use `bun install --frozen-lockfile` before qualification. Keep `package.json` and `or3.manifest.json` on the same fresh version for each new artifact; a different archive with changed bytes needs a new version before release. This package is private and is installed through OR3's reviewed package flow, not the creator's build-time provider version map.
